{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-higher-forms","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:higher-forms","kind":"definition","title":"Higher differential forms","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-universe"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-higher-forms-su2"],"tags":["differential-forms","category-theory"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.HigherForms","text":"higher-forms.md","leanSource":"higher-forms.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:higher-forms\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a <a href=\"#def:quantum-universe\" data-at=\"quantum-universes/quantum-universe\">quantum universe</a> with differential calculus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega^1(A)</code>. The <strong>higher differential forms</strong> are the graded <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>-bimodule:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Omega^k(A) =  \\bigwedge\\nolimits_A^k \\Omega^1(A), \\qquad k = 0, 1, 2, \\ldots</code></pre>\n<p>Here <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega^0(A) = A</code>. For an object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda^k V</code> denotes its <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code>-th exterior power. The differential <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d \\colon \\Omega^k(A) \\to \\Omega^{k+1}(A)</code> extends the universal derivation by the graded Leibniz rule and satisfies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d^2 = 0</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"tex-ph\"><strong>[Diagram]</strong><details><summary>LaTeX source</summary><pre>\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:de-rham-complex}\n\\begin{tikzcd}[column sep=2.5em]\n  A = \\Omega^0(A) \\ar[r, &quot;d&quot;]\n  &amp; \\Omega^1(A) \\ar[r, &quot;d&quot;]\n  &amp; \\Omega^2(A) \\ar[r, &quot;d&quot;]\n  &amp; \\cdots\n\\end{tikzcd}\n\\qquad (d^2 = 0)\n\\end{equation}</pre></details></div>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/higher-forms.md","heading":"Definition","number":"3.4.5","page":"b/def-higher-forms","qa":{"counts":{"pass":83,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":56},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.HigherForms","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/higher-forms.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
